ficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320780/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de6dbad-0ca5-5a17-a04b-cdfd72d6dab5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320780"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320776/field-1/cb0338e04ce3e095f1a22dbf46c6fa9e63b849036c96f43377fbbf995b12ce6b" :answer/id #uuid "4cfacf4c-3657-5b44-9f8e-064e23dfbf7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(3c+5i)(3c-5i)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320776/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f09fc79a-bdfc-562e-a8dd-0814dc4d683d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320776/field-1/cb0338e04ce3e095f1a22dbf46c6fa9e63b849036c96f43377fbbf995b12ce6b" :answer-field/choices ["q-320776/field-1/cb0338e04ce3e095f1a22dbf46c6fa9e63b849036c96f43377fbbf995b12ce6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320776" :question/id #uuid "a5380849-083c-5460-8e52-ea0790b87768" :question/math-academy-id "q-320776" :question/problem "Write $18{c}^{2}+50$ in factored form by rewriting the second term of the expression as the square of an imaginary number. Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$18{c}^{2}+50=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor out $2$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n18{c}^{2}+50=2\\,(9{c}^{2}+25).\n$$\n\nNow focus on factoring $(9{c}^{2}+25).$  \n\nTo factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor it as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{c}^{2}+25 & =9{c}^{2}-(-25) \\\\  & =9{c}^{2}-(25{i}^{2}) \\\\  & =(3c)^{2}-(5i)^{2} \\\\  & =(3c+5i)(3c-5i).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting back, we obtain\n\n$$\n2\\,(9{c}^{2}+25)=2(3c+5i)(3c-5i).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320776/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de6dbad-0ca5-5a17-a04b-cdfd72d6dab5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320776"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-367715/field-1/59991b804d9335848629522889e9fa538efbaeb45cd16b73cd164918a45979e3" :answer/id #uuid "e56ff8b8-9576-5051-919f-a12a250b9105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3y+i)^2(3y-i)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-367715/field-1/d638e5995705fcf47307cabf8cc0b32b385fac8e5a3c18b1b7fc394730c8bbc0" :answer/id #uuid "851007e2-763f-57b2-aa96-add36f217aa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3y+1)^2(3y-1)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-367715/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "83e671b5-5d29-546b-a844-31729b46cfba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-367715/field-1/59991b804d9335848629522889e9fa538efbaeb45cd16b73cd164918a45979e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-367715/field-1/59991b804d9335848629522889e9fa538efbaeb45cd16b73cd164918a45979e3" "q-367715/field-1/d638e5995705fcf47307cabf8cc0b32b385fac8e5a3c18b1b7fc394730c8bbc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-367715" :question/id #uuid "6b680876-de58-5871-8a5a-95c40df18679" :question/math-academy-id "q-367715" :question/problem "Write $81{y}^{4}+18{y}^{2}+1$ in factored form as $(a+bi)^{2}(a-bi)^{2}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$81{y}^{4}+18{y}^{2}+1=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${y}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}81{y}^{4}+18{y}^{2}+1 & ={(9{y}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot (9{y}^{2})\\cdot 1+{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={(9{y}^{2}+1)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}+1 & =9{y}^{2}-(-1) \\\\  & =9{y}^{2}-({i}^{2}) \\\\  & ={(3y)}^{2}-{(i)}^{2} \\\\  & =(3y+i)(3y-i)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our main expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}81{y}^{4}+18{y}^{2}+1 & ={(9{y}^{2}+1)}^{2} \\\\  & ={((3y+i)(3y-i))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(3y+i)}^{2}{(3y-i)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-367715/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c55fcfa4-0050-5a80-a142-29616155797f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-367715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-389797/field-1/cfcb5f618652f0fa7e563699ec580bc517add55b23c147d026b2648d96467556" :answer/id #uuid "008ec3df-d702-5bf1-acbd-3abbc0b78538" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+5i)^2(x-5i)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-389797/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f54a709a-63f3-5f2c-861f-7391085d7b3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-389797/field-1/cfcb5f618652f0fa7e563699ec580bc517add55b23c147d026b2648d96467556" :answer-field/choices ["q-389797/field-1/cfcb5f618652f0fa7e563699ec580bc517add55b23c147d026b2648d96467556"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-389797" :question/id #uuid "710681dd-b391-58c3-8b1b-c34afdb4e6f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-389797" :question/problem "Write ${x}^{4}+50{x}^{2}+625$ in factored form as $(a+bi)^{2}(a-bi)^{2}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n${x}^{4}+50{x}^{2}+625=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${x}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}+50{x}^{2}+625 & ={({x}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot 25\\cdot ({x}^{2})+{25}^{2} \\\\  & ={({x}^{2}+25)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+25 & ={x}^{2}-(-25) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-(25{i}^{2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-{(5i)}^{2} \\\\  & =(x+5i)(x-5i)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our main expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}+50{x}^{2}+625 & ={({x}^{2}+25)}^{2} \\\\  & ={((x+5i)(x-5i))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(x+5i)}^{2}{(x-5i)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-389797/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c55fcfa4-0050-5a80-a142-29616155797f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-389797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319471/field-1/836d93966c1b46efdf6c0cbb3e9df63817ee412fdd753e1a52c25fa79593629b" :answer/id #uuid "ad1d89d9-d173-52a5-856a-509ac9175566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+i\\sqrt{5})^2(x-i\\sqrt{5})^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319471/field-1/cfcb5f618652f0fa7e563699ec580bc517add55b23c147d026b2648d96467556" :answer/id #uuid "06cd9553-b8ee-5272-870f-8c369d280282" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+5i)^2(x-5i)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319471/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2166193f-e9df-5425-a134-4e68c5f74e91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319471/field-1/836d93966c1b46efdf6c0cbb3e9df63817ee412fdd753e1a52c25fa79593629b" :answer-field/choices ["q-319471/field-1/836d93966c1b46efdf6c0cbb3e9df63817ee412fdd753e1a52c25fa79593629b" "q-319471/field-1/cfcb5f618652f0fa7e563699ec580bc517add55b23c147d026b2648d96467556"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319471" :question/id #uuid "15785172-c630-5198-be0a-963b458e2faa" :question/math-academy-id "q-319471" :question/problem "Write ${x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+25$ in factored form as $(a+bi)^{2}(a-bi)^{2}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n${x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+25=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${x}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+25 & ={({x}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot ({x}^{2})+{5}^{2} \\\\  & ={({x}^{2}+5)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5 & ={x}^{2}-(-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-(5{i}^{2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-{(\\sqrt{5}\\,i)}^{2} \\\\  & =(x+\\sqrt{5}\\,i)(x-\\sqrt{5}\\,i)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our main expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+25 & ={({x}^{2}+5)}^{2} \\\\  & ={((x+\\sqrt{5}\\,i)(x-\\sqrt{5}\\,i))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(x+\\sqrt{5}\\,i)}^{2}{(x-\\sqrt{5}\\,i)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-319471/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c55fcfa4-0050-5a80-a142-29616155797f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319471"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320891/field-1/4228f11824dc9fc6cf57202f4a48a4e9561da6b475e3cbc421bc47ee12ed4378" :answer/id #uuid "f0f3cda6-0426-5ef3-9ecb-780293a71e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2x+i)^2(2x-i)^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320891/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ba2619c-c113-5f6d-9e5f-6d1217e53f3a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320891/field-1/4228f11824dc9fc6cf57202f4a48a4e9561da6b475e3cbc421bc47ee12ed4378" :answer-field/choices ["q-320891/field-1/4228f11824dc9fc6cf57202f4a48a4e9561da6b475e3cbc421bc47ee12ed4378"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320891" :question/id #uuid "a780393b-b1a4-5e5d-8b0b-c78216aed36b" :question/math-academy-id "q-320891" :question/problem "Write $16{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+1$ in factored form as $(a+bi)^{2}(a-bi)^{2}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$16{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+1=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${b}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+1 & ={(4{x}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot (4{x}^{2})\\cdot 1+{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={(4{x}^{2}+1)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+1 & =4{x}^{2}-(-1) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-({i}^{2}) \\\\  & ={(2x)}^{2}-{(i)}^{2} \\\\  & =(2x+i)(2x-i)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our main expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+1 & ={(4{x}^{2}+1)}^{2} \\\\  & ={((2x+i)(2x-i))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(2x+i)}^{2}{(2x-i)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-320891/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c55fcfa4-0050-5a80-a142-29616155797f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170501/selection/e42698f7fc1e0cf6e1dded8cef5dc3850457adef1bdf13c5f6aef8d91db3d621" :answer/id #uuid "f3db476d-337a-5742-986b-07e3d6c742b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\sqrt{3}t+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})^{2}(\\sqrt{3}t-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170501/selection/26be01d99f7011417d923d32862c47afae8cb1126c8476f9eaa87e59bbac0573" :answer/id #uuid "c26b584a-58cd-5c24-af0b-00b6578c622b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9(t+\\sqrt{5})^{2}(t-\\sqrt{5})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170501/selection/ff512da09d83e6368ebca825aa8806ade9e6dcaea8f7c21c778254d75291df6d" :answer/id #uuid "28836f53-20b3-5352-9dba-70756d09472e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\sqrt{3}t+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170501/selection/3c502269351bb3d5e4e6a205c242d5d78a572bc0e6815f5f36c3fad5cb95a0d6" :answer/id #uuid "16ee580c-25f9-59f9-9050-40166c47d38e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3t+5\\text{i})^{2}(3t-5\\text{i})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170501/selection/954c53501745d2c92de77bc264663336e0a9bdb6a6f117defbdfcc81b470d2cb" :answer/id #uuid "5d84227a-3f31-552c-9b98-eba9e55e2c45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\sqrt{3}t+\\sqrt{5})^{2}(\\sqrt{3}t-\\sqrt{5})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170501/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b8d6efa-3171-55f1-848f-4a2c01829e74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170501/selection/e42698f7fc1e0cf6e1dded8cef5dc3850457adef1bdf13c5f6aef8d91db3d621" :answer-field/choices ["q-170501/selection/e42698f7fc1e0cf6e1dded8cef5dc3850457adef1bdf13c5f6aef8d91db3d621" "q-170501/selection/26be01d99f7011417d923d32862c47afae8cb1126c8476f9eaa87e59bbac0573" "q-170501/selection/ff512da09d83e6368ebca825aa8806ade9e6dcaea8f7c21c778254d75291df6d" "q-170501/selection/3c502269351bb3d5e4e6a205c242d5d78a572bc0e6815f5f36c3fad5cb95a0d6" "q-170501/selection/954c53501745d2c92de77bc264663336e0a9bdb6a6f117defbdfcc81b470d2cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170501" :question/id #uuid "21e2d89f-0660-5a0d-981b-df2f4731097d" :question/math-academy-id "q-170501" :question/problem "Factor $9{t}^{4}+30{t}^{2}+25.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${t}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{t}^{4}+30{t}^{2}+25 & ={(3{t}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot (3{t}^{2})\\cdot 5+{5}^{2} \\\\  & =(3{t}^{2}+5)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+5 & =3{t}^{2}-(-5) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-(5{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{3}t)^{2}-(\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})^{2} \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{3}t+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})(\\sqrt{3}t-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our main expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{t}^{4}+30{t}^{2}+25 & =(3{t}^{2}+5)^{2} \\\\  & =((\\sqrt{3}t+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})(\\sqrt{3}t-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}))^{2} \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{3}t+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})^{2}(\\sqrt{3}t-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-170501/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c55fcfa4-0050-5a80-a142-29616155797f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170501"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
